  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support programme for victims of psychological suffering in Rwanda - CDJP Kigali</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Justice and Peace Commission of the archdiocese of Kigali is one of the two structures of Catholic Church involved in the programme to bring in their expertise in conflict resolution and their large implantation in the country side. After being trained in trauma healing elementary knowledge, their paralegals demonstrated an added value in peace and reconciliation taking into account the mental health of the beneficiaries. 

In 2008, they planned the building of two playing grounds to promote social and community cohesion, trainings: for 40 paralegals, 60 new APS, for 60 church and community leaders at parish and basic level. A stepping stones training session for community is planned to be done by trainers trained in the first year.  Counselling sessions for beneficiaries and clinical supervision are planned for all trauma professionals.</narrative>
  </description>
